---
/**
 * Theme builder: an accent per scheme or one for all three (a candy, or any colour with its light and shade worked
 * out and nudged until ink labels read), a pixel size, a live preview, contrast checks that hold the export back
 * when they fail, warnings when the accent looks like an intent or like focus, and the result as DTCG token files
 * and CSS. Then the same by hand: which roles, in which blocks, in which layer, read from the tokens.
 */
import Docs from "../../layouts/Docs.astro";
import Icon from "../../components/Icon.astro";
import Table from "../../components/Table.astro";
import { manifest, read, schemeBlocks, tokens } from "../../lib/data";
import { SCHEMES } from "../../lib/colour";
import { codeBlock } from "../../lib/markdown";
import { code } from "../../lib/html";

const t = tokens();
// The candies that can be an accent: Liquorice (slate) is not one, its labels are white (DESIGN.md, Colors).
const CANDIES = ["blue", "teal", "green", "purple", "pink", "red", "orange"];
const candies = Object.fromEntries(CANDIES.map((c) => [c, { base: t.shared[`candy-${c}`], light: t.shared[`candy-${c}-light`], shade: t.shared[`candy-${c}-shade`] }]));
const DEFAULTS: Record<string, string> = { day: "blue", sunset: "pink", night: "purple" };
const schemes = Object.fromEntries(SCHEMES.map((s) => [s.id, {
  title: s.title,
  dark: s.id === "night",
  bg: t.schemes[s.id].bg, surface: t.schemes[s.id].surface, raised: t.schemes[s.id]["surface-raised"], dither: t.schemes[s.id]["disabled-dither"],
  accent: { candy: DEFAULTS[s.id], base: t.schemes[s.id].accent, light: t.schemes[s.id]["accent-light"], shade: t.schemes[s.id]["accent-shade"], text: t.schemes[s.id]["accent-text"], on: t.schemes[s.id]["accent-on"] },
}]));
// What an accent must not look like: the intents (the same candies in every scheme) and the focus ring's yellow.
const intents = {
  danger: { name: "danger", base: t.schemes.day.danger, candy: "Gumball Red", why: "Red is danger in Blip: destructive actions, errors and invalid fields.", reads: "destructive" },
  warning: { name: "a warning", base: t.schemes.day.warning, candy: "Sherbet Orange", why: "Orange is warning in Blip (yellow is taken by focus).", reads: "a warning" },
  success: { name: "success", base: t.schemes.day.success, candy: "Sour Apple", why: "Green is success in Blip: done, saved, cleared.", reads: "done" },
};
const blocks = schemeBlocks();
const data = { candies, schemes, ink: t.shared.ink, white: t.shared.white, focus: t.schemes.day.focus, intents, blocks };

// ------------------------------------------------------------------ by hand: the roles, the blocks, the layer

const ROLES: [string, string, string][] = [
  ["accent", "The candy: the main button, the chosen tab, a checked box, the progress fill.", "Its label, 4.5:1"],
  ["accent-light", "The light band, and the whole fill of soft boxes and of chosen outline and ghost ones.", "Its label, and selected text (ink), 4.5:1"],
  ["accent-shade", "The shade band, and the top band of a box that is chosen.", "Nothing: no text sits on it"],
  ["accent-text", "The accent as text: links, the caret, the chosen underline tab.", `4.5:1 on ${["bg", "surface", "surface-raised"].map((r) => `--pp-${r}`).join(", ")}`],
  ["accent-on", "Labels and icons on the candy and on the soft fill.", "4.5:1 on both, and on a disabled button's dither (--pp-disabled-dither): ink, on any candy that takes ink"],
  ["selection-bg", "Selected text, behind ink (--pp-selection-text): the light band again.", "Ink on it, 4.5:1"],
];
const known = new Map(manifest().map((m) => [m.name, m]));
for (const [role] of ROLES) if (!known.has(role)) throw new Error(`docs: the theme page names --pp-${role}, which the tokens no longer have`);
const roleRows = ROLES.map(([role, what, must]) => [code(known.get(role)!.cssVar), what, must.replace(/(--pp-[a-z-]+)/g, (m) => code(m))]);
const valueOf = (scheme: string, role: string) => t.schemes[scheme as "day"][role];
const recipeLines = ["/* After @jaatster/blip-tokens/tokens.css */", "@layer pp.tokens {"];
for (const b of blocks) {
  const pad = "  ".repeat(b.wrap.length + 1);
  b.wrap.forEach((w, i) => recipeLines.push(`${"  ".repeat(i + 1)}${w} {`));
  recipeLines.push(`${pad}${b.selector} {`, ...ROLES.map(([role]) => `${pad}  ${known.get(role)!.cssVar}: ${valueOf(b.scheme, role)};`), `${pad}}`);
  b.wrap.forEach((_, i) => recipeLines.push(`${"  ".repeat(b.wrap.length - i)}}`));
}
recipeLines.push("}");
const recipe = await codeBlock(recipeLines.join("\n"), "css", "my-theme.css");
// @jaatster/blip-tokens' command (its README): builds the theme's tokens.css through Blip's checks.
const cli = await codeBlock(`npx blip-tokens my-theme.resolver.json                # writes my-theme.css beside it
npx blip-tokens my-theme.resolver.json --out src/tokens.css
npx blip-tokens my-theme.resolver.json --check        # checks only, writes nothing`, "sh", "Shell");
const screenOnly = blocks.filter((b) => b.wrap.some((w) => /^@media screen\b/.test(w))).map((b) => b.scheme);
// Which of the roles tokens.css registers with @property (as colours).
const registered = ROLES.map(([role]) => known.get(role)!.cssVar).filter((v) => new RegExp(`@property ${v} \\{[^}]*<color>`).test(read("packages/tokens/dist/css/tokens.css")));
const H = (id: string, text: string) => ({ depth: 2, id, text });
---
<Docs title="Theme builder" description="Make a Blip theme: an accent for each time of day, nudged until every label passes AA, a pixel size, a live preview with contrast checks, exported as DTCG tokens and CSS, or written by hand." wide styles={["theme"]} scripts={["theme"]} headings={[H("tb-controls-title", "Your theme"), H("tb-preview-title", "Preview"), H("tb-export-title", "Export"), H("by-hand", "By hand")]}>
  <header class="docs-page-head tb-head">
    <h1 class="docs-page-title pp-display" data-scale="2">Theme builder</h1>
    <p class="docs-lede">Pick an accent for each time of day, from the candies or any colour you like, and a pixel size. The light and shade bands are worked out the way the candies' were, a colour too dark or too pale for ink labels is nudged until they read, and the result comes out as token files for the resolver and as CSS.</p>
  </header>

  <noscript><p class="pp-box pp-alert" data-tone="info"><span class="pp-alert-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span><span class="pp-alert-body">The builder needs JavaScript. To set an accent by hand, see <a href="#by-hand">By hand</a> below; the candies and the scheme roles are all on <a href="/foundations/colour/">Colour</a>.</span></p></noscript>

  <div class="tb docs-needs-js">
    <section class="pp-box tb-controls" data-variant="panel" aria-labelledby="tb-controls-title">
      <h2 class="tb-h2" id="tb-controls-title">Your theme</h2>

      <div class="tb-field">
        <span class="pp-label" id="tb-scheme-label">Time of day</span>
        <pp-segmented class="pp-box pp-segmented tb-scheme" aria-labelledby="tb-scheme-label" value="day" data-width="full">
          {SCHEMES.map((s, i) => <button class="pp-box" type="button" value={s.id} aria-checked={i === 0 ? "true" : "false"}><Icon name={s.id === "day" ? "sun" : s.id === "sunset" ? "sunset" : "moon"} />{s.title}</button>)}
        </pp-segmented>
        <label class="pp-check" data-layout="split">One accent for all three<span class="pp-box pp-switch"><input type="checkbox" role="switch" class="pp-box tb-all" aria-describedby="tb-all-help" /></span></label>
        <p class="pp-check-help" id="tb-all-help">On, a pick sets Day, Sunset and Night at once; the accent text still changes with each, to read on its surfaces.</p>
      </div>

      <fieldset class="tb-field tb-candies">
        <legend class="pp-label">Accent for <span class="tb-scheme-name">Day</span></legend>
        <div class="tb-swatches" role="radiogroup" aria-label="Candy">
          {CANDIES.map((c) => (
            <label class="pp-box tb-swatch" data-tone={c} title={c}>
              <input type="radio" name="tb-candy" value={c} />
              <span class="pp-sr-only">{c}</span>
              <span class="tb-swatch-mark" aria-hidden="true"></span>
            </label>
          ))}
        </div>
      </fieldset>

      <div class="tb-field">
        <label class="pp-label" for="tb-hex">Or any colour</label>
        <div class="tb-hex-row">
          <span class="pp-box pp-input tb-hex"><input id="tb-hex" type="text" inputmode="text" spellcheck="false" autocomplete="off" maxlength="7" value="#33A3FF" aria-describedby="tb-hex-help" /></span>
          <input class="tb-picker" type="color" value="#33a3ff" aria-label="Pick a colour" />
        </div>
        <p class="pp-field-help" id="tb-hex-help">A base colour. Light: 0.65 of its saturation at full brightness. Shade: 0.84 of its brightness.</p>
        <div class="tb-warnings" aria-live="polite"></div>
      </div>

      <div class="tb-field">
        <span class="pp-label">The candy, worked out</span>
        <div class="tb-derived">
          <span class="pp-box tb-derived-box" aria-hidden="true"></span>
          <dl class="tb-derived-values">
            <div><dt>Light</dt><dd><span class="tb-dot" data-k="light"></span><code data-v="light"></code><span class="tb-from" data-from="light"></span></dd></div>
            <div><dt>Base</dt><dd><span class="tb-dot" data-k="base"></span><code data-v="base"></code><span class="tb-from" data-from="base"></span></dd></div>
            <div><dt>Shade</dt><dd><span class="tb-dot" data-k="shade"></span><code data-v="shade"></code></dd></div>
            <div><dt>Text</dt><dd><span class="tb-dot" data-k="text"></span><code data-v="text"></code></dd></div>
            <div><dt>Label</dt><dd><span class="tb-dot" data-k="on"></span><code data-v="on"></code></dd></div>
          </dl>
        </div>
        <p class="pp-small tb-nudge" aria-live="polite" hidden></p>
        <label class="pp-check tb-exact-row" data-layout="split" hidden>Keep my exact colour<span class="pp-box pp-switch"><input type="checkbox" role="switch" class="pp-box tb-exact" /></span></label>
      </div>

      <div class="tb-field">
        <span class="pp-label" id="tb-checks-title">Contrast</span>
        <ul class="tb-checks" role="list" aria-labelledby="tb-checks-title"></ul>
        <p class="pp-small tb-summary" role="status"></p>
      </div>

      <div class="tb-field">
        <span class="pp-label" id="tb-pixel-label">Pixel</span>
        <pp-segmented class="pp-box pp-segmented tb-pixel" aria-labelledby="tb-pixel-label" value="2">
          <button class="pp-box" type="button" value="2" aria-checked="true">2 px</button>
          <button class="pp-box" type="button" value="3">3 px</button>
          <button class="pp-box" type="button" value="4">4 px</button>
        </pp-segmented>
      </div>

      <button class="pp-box pp-button tb-reset" type="button" data-variant="ghost" data-size="sm"><Icon name="undo" />Back to Blip's own</button>
    </section>

    <section class="tb-preview-wrap" aria-labelledby="tb-preview-title">
      <h2 class="tb-h2" id="tb-preview-title">Preview</h2>
      <div class="tb-strip" aria-hidden="true">
        {SCHEMES.map((s) => <div class="tb-strip-cell" data-pp-scheme={s.id} data-strip={s.id}><span class="pp-box pp-button" data-size="sm">{s.title}</span><span class="pp-box pp-button" data-size="sm" data-variant="soft">Soft</span></div>)}
      </div>
      <div class="tb-preview-scroll docs-scroll">
        <div class="tb-preview" data-pp-scheme="day">
          <div class="pp-box tb-sample" data-variant="panel">
            <div class="tb-sample-head">
              <p class="pp-display pp-pop" data-scale="2" data-pop="Level 2">Level 2</p>
              <span class="pp-box pp-badge" data-size="sm">New</span>
            </div>
            <div class="pp-tabs" data-variant="soft" data-size="sm">
              <div class="pp-tabs-list" role="tablist" aria-label="Sample tabs">
                <button class="pp-box pp-tab" data-variant="soft" role="tab" aria-selected="true" type="button">Play</button>
                <button class="pp-box pp-tab" data-variant="soft" role="tab" aria-selected="false" type="button" tabindex="-1">Map</button>
                <button class="pp-box pp-tab" data-variant="soft" role="tab" aria-selected="false" type="button" tabindex="-1">Items</button>
              </div>
            </div>
            <p class="pp-body">Your theme's accent, in the parts that use it: candy and soft buttons, the chosen tab, a switch, a checkbox, the progress fill, POP letters and <a href="#tb-preview-title">a link like this one</a>.</p>
            <div class="docs-row">
              <button class="pp-box pp-button" type="button">Continue</button>
              <button class="pp-box pp-button" type="button" data-variant="soft">Options</button>
              <button class="pp-box pp-button" type="button" data-variant="outline" aria-pressed="true">Outline, on</button>
            </div>
            <div class="docs-row tb-focus-row">
              <button class="pp-box pp-button" type="button" data-pp-state="focus" tabindex="-1">Focused</button>
              <span class="pp-small pp-muted">The focus ring, beside your candy.</span>
            </div>
            <div class="tb-sample-row">
              <label class="pp-check"><span class="pp-box pp-checkbox"><input type="checkbox" checked /></span>Auto-save</label>
              <label class="pp-check"><span class="pp-box pp-switch"><input type="checkbox" role="switch" class="pp-box" checked /></span>Music</label>
              <span class="pp-box pp-tag">Rare</span>
            </div>
            <div>
              <div class="pp-progress-label"><label for="tb-progress">World 2</label><span>60%</span></div>
              <div class="pp-box pp-progress"><progress id="tb-progress" max="100" value="60">60%</progress></div>
            </div>
            <pp-segmented class="pp-box pp-segmented" data-size="sm" aria-label="Difficulty" value="normal">
              <button class="pp-box" type="button" value="easy">Easy</button>
              <button class="pp-box" type="button" value="normal" aria-checked="true">Normal</button>
              <button class="pp-box" type="button" value="hard">Hard</button>
            </pp-segmented>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="tb-export" aria-labelledby="tb-export-title">
      <h2 class="tb-h2" id="tb-export-title">Export</h2>
      <p class="docs-note">Two ways to use it. The CSS goes after Blip's <code class="docs-inline-code">tokens.css</code>, as it is. Or build a checked <code class="docs-inline-code">tokens.css</code> of your own: put the token files and the resolver in your project's folder, beside <code class="docs-inline-code">node_modules</code>, and run <code class="docs-inline-code">blip-tokens</code>, which checks every pair as Blip's own tokens are checked, and writes a file to load instead of Blip's.</p>
      <Fragment set:html={cli} />
      <div class="pp-box pp-alert tb-blocked" data-tone="danger" role="group" aria-labelledby="tb-blocked-title" hidden>
        <span class="pp-alert-icon" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <div class="pp-alert-body">
          <p class="pp-alert-title" id="tb-blocked-title">Some labels would not pass AA</p>
          <ul class="tb-blocked-list"></ul>
          <p>Pick another colour, or turn off "Keep my exact colour" to have it nudged. Or export it as it is, and check those pairs yourself:</p>
          <label class="pp-check"><span class="pp-box pp-checkbox" data-tone="danger"><input type="checkbox" class="tb-override" /></span>Export anyway</label>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p class="pp-small tb-downloaded" role="status"></p>
      <pp-tabs class="pp-tabs" data-variant="underline" data-size="sm">
        <div class="pp-tabs-list" role="tablist" aria-label="Export formats">
          <button class="pp-box pp-tab" data-variant="ghost" role="tab" aria-selected="true" type="button">CSS</button>
          <button class="pp-box pp-tab" data-variant="ghost" role="tab" aria-selected="false" type="button" tabindex="-1">Day tokens</button>
          <button class="pp-box pp-tab" data-variant="ghost" role="tab" aria-selected="false" type="button" tabindex="-1">Sunset tokens</button>
          <button class="pp-box pp-tab" data-variant="ghost" role="tab" aria-selected="false" type="button" tabindex="-1">Night tokens</button>
          <button class="pp-box pp-tab" data-variant="ghost" role="tab" aria-selected="false" type="button" tabindex="-1">Resolver</button>
        </div>
        {[["css", "my-theme.css", "CSS"], ["day", "my-theme.day.tokens.json", "JSON"], ["sunset", "my-theme.sunset.tokens.json", "JSON"], ["night", "my-theme.night.tokens.json", "JSON"], ["resolver", "my-theme.resolver.json", "JSON"]].map(([id, file, lang], i) => (
          <div class="pp-tabs-panel" role="tabpanel" hidden={i > 0 ? true : undefined}>
            <figure class="pp-box docs-code tb-out">
              <figcaption class="docs-code-bar">
                <span class="docs-code-lang">{file}</span>
                <span class="docs-row tb-out-actions">
                  <button class="pp-box pp-button docs-copy" type="button" data-variant="ghost" data-size="sm" data-copy-from={`#tb-out-${id}`}>Copy</button>
                  <button class="pp-box pp-button tb-download" type="button" data-variant="soft" data-size="sm" data-file={file} data-from={`#tb-out-${id}`}><Icon name="download" />Download</button>
                </span>
              </figcaption>
              <pre class="tb-code" data-lang={lang} tabindex="0" aria-label={file}><code id={`tb-out-${id}`}></code></pre>
            </figure>
          </div>
        ))}
      </pp-tabs>
    </section>
  </div>

  <section class="docs-section tb-by-hand" aria-labelledby="by-hand">
    <h2 id="by-hand">By hand</h2>
    <p>An accent is six scheme roles. Set them the way <code class="docs-inline-code">tokens.css</code> sets its own: inside <code class="docs-inline-code">@layer pp.tokens</code>, with the same selectors, in a file loaded after it. Same layer, same selectors and later, so yours win exactly where Blip's would. A rule outside the layer would beat every scheme at once: an unlayered <code class="docs-inline-code">:root</code> rule turns Sunset and Night to your Day.</p>
    <Table label="The accent's roles" head={["Role", "What it paints", "Must pass"]} rows={roleRows} />
    <p>Here they are with Blip's own values, in every block <code class="docs-inline-code">tokens.css</code> has for them: Day, which is also a page with no scheme set; Sunset; Night; and Night again, for a page with no scheme that follows a device in dark mode.{screenOnly.length > 0 && ` As in tokens.css, ${screenOnly.includes("sunset") ? "Sunset and " : ""}Night ${screenOnly.includes("sunset") ? "are" : "is"} for screens only: a printed page uses Day's.`}</p>
    <Fragment set:html={recipe} />
    <ul class="docs-help">
      {registered.length > 0 && <li><Fragment set:html={registered.map((r) => code(r)).join(", ")} /> {registered.length === 1 ? "is" : "are"} registered as {registered.length === 1 ? "a colour" : "colours"} (<code class="docs-inline-code">@property</code> in <code class="docs-inline-code">tokens.css</code>): give {registered.length === 1 ? "it" : "them"} a colour, or a <code class="docs-inline-code">var()</code> that holds one.</li>}
      <li>Nothing checks a CSS file. Put each block's colours into the builder, or write them as token files and run <code class="docs-inline-code">blip-tokens</code> on them (see Export, above): it checks every pair in the table and stops on the first that fails.</li>
      <li>The info intent is the Day accent's blue in every scheme, and stays so. The other intents (success, warning, danger) are separate roles; an accent close to one of them makes every main button look like it.</li>
    </ul>
  </section>

  <script type="application/json" id="tb-data" set:html={JSON.stringify(data)} />
</Docs>
